Yeah.
是啊。

506
00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:16.980
And we had all this dialogue where they wanted us to just reminisce about our relationship.
我们当时有很多对话，他们想让我们回忆一下我们的感情经历。

507
00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:20.640
And I can't remember if that was improvised or if that was written.
我不记得那是即兴发挥的，还是剧本里写好的。

508
00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:21.560
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

509
00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:27.640
Well, guess who's going to go to the shooting draft and see?
好吧，猜猜谁要去查剧本看看？

510
00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:29.000
You'll let us know.
你会告诉我们的。

511
00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.060
Launch party.
发布会派对。

512
00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.120
I'm going to look in the candy bags.
我要去看看糖果袋里有什么。

513
00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:34.940
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

514
00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:35.820
Yep.
没错。

515
00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:36.600
Wowzers.
哇哦。

516
00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:37.200
Okay.
好吧。

517
00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.540
I don't even know where we were.
我都不记得我们刚才说到哪了。

518
00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:41.660
Oh, my other favorite Pam moment.
噢，我另一个最喜欢的帕姆高光时刻。

519
00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:46.120
The whole reason I'm wearing the shirt that says Pam Sass.
我穿这件写着“帕姆毒舌”衬衫的全部原因。

520
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:52.140
Because I could not do an all about Pam Beasley and not talk about her Pam Sass.
因为我做一期关于帕姆·比斯利的节目，不可能不聊聊她的毒舌。

521
00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:53.680
It's one of my favorite things.
这是我最喜欢的事情之一。

522
00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:56.380
It is a runner throughout the entire series.
这是贯穿整部剧的一个梗。

523
00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:59.720
And we got a fan mail flurry about it.
我们收到了很多关于这个的粉丝来信。

524
00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:02.980
People really wanted us to share some Pam Sass.
大家真的很想让我们分享一些帕姆的毒舌时刻。

525
00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:04.980
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

526
00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:09.620
But as it turns out, there are a ton of Pam Sass video compilations online.
结果发现，网上有成堆的帕姆毒舌合集视频。

527
00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:09.910
There are?
真的吗？

528
00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.120
There are so many.
真的有很多。

529
00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:18.380
One of my favorites that I watched in prepping for this episode was titled The Best of Pam's Brutal Comebacks.
我在为这集节目做准备时看的一个最喜欢的视频，标题是《帕姆最强毒舌回击集锦》。

530
00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:20.500
I mean, that's a great title.
我是说，这标题太棒了。

531
00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:23.000
Here are just a few I'm going to play.
我这就放几个片段给大家听听。

532
00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:24.700
I'm also going to read some.
我也会读一些出来。

533
00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.180
Let's start with Pam versus Kevin.
我们先从帕姆对阵凯文开始。

534
00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:30.640
Pam, when will the new copier be ready?
帕姆，新复印机什么时候能好？

535
00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:31.840
I'm working on it, Kev.
我正在弄，凯文。

536
00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:33.780
You said it would be ready by today.
你说过今天就能好的。

537
00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:35.620
And it is today.
现在就是今天啊。

538
00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:37.300
It'll be ready soon.
很快就会好的。

539
00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:38.760
Soon could mean anything.
“很快”可能意味着任何时间。

540
00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:40.880
Soon could be three weeks.
“很快”可能是三周。

541
00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:43.200
Is that what soon means to you?
这就是你理解的“很快”吗？

542
00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:44.840
Sometimes.
有时候是。

543
00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:46.660
Then come back soon.
那你就“很快”再回来吧。

544
00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:50.360
I mean the sass.
我是说，这毒舌劲儿。

545
00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:51.880
That was pretty good.
那段真不错。

546
00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:53.800
Is that what soon means to you?
这就是你理解的“很快”吗？

547
00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:57.100
Okay, now Pam versus Todd Packer.
好了，现在是帕姆对阵托德·帕克。

548
00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:00.720
Don't ever let this little bitch drive you around town.
永远别让这个小婊子开车带你在城里转。

549
00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:02.280
We got lost for half an hour.
我们迷路了半个小时。

550
00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.520
I don't have any DUIs, so I can drive myself.
我可没有酒驾记录，所以我可以自己开车。

551
00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:05.060
But thanks.
但还是谢谢你。

552
00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:07.460
But thanks.
但还是谢谢你。

553
00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:09.500
That's kind of like Pam's bless your heart.
这有点像帕姆说的“愿上帝保佑你”。

554
00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:10.200
But thanks.
但还是谢谢你。

555
00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:10.940
Yeah.
是啊。

556
00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:16.880
Then there is the Halloween episode when Jim makes fun of her for believing in ghosts.
还有万圣节那一集，吉姆取笑帕姆相信有鬼。

557
00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:19.980
And then Pam says she'll draw a picture of the ghost for Jim.
然后帕姆说她要给吉姆画一张鬼的画像。

558
00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:22.180
And she just draws the middle finger.
结果她画了个中指。

559
00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:23.220
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

560
00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:24.180
Flips him off.
对他竖中指。

561
00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:24.800
That's right.
没错。

562
00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:28.480
But maybe the biggest category for Pam's sass.
但帕姆毒舌最精彩的类别可能还是这个。

563
00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:30.560
And honestly, this could be a whole show.
老实说，这都能单独做一档节目了。

564
00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.280
Is it Pam versus Ryan?
是帕姆对战瑞安吗？

565
00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.200
You betcha.
你说对了。

566
00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.060
It's my favorite.
这是我的最爱。

567
00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:38.100
There are so many clips of Pam and Ryan going head to head.
帕姆和瑞安针锋相对的片段太多了。

568
00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:38.960
That's so great.
太棒了。

569
00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.260
It was really hard to choose.
真的很难选。

570
00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:42.320
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

571
00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:43.540
This might be my favorite.
这可能是我最喜欢的一个。

572
00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:46.680
Also, little tip.
另外，给个小贴士。

573
00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:48.120
Never shake the baby.
千万别摇晃婴儿。

574
00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:50.520
Sorry, just to be clear.
抱歉，确认一下。

575
00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:51.980
You're saying do not shake the baby.
你是说不要摇晃婴儿。

576
00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:52.640
Don't shake the baby.
不要摇晃婴儿。

577
00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:58.260
A lot of times parents get frustrated because the baby's crying and they shake the baby.
很多时候父母因为婴儿哭闹而感到沮丧，就会去摇晃婴儿。

578
00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:00.320
And you got to, you can't do that.
你必须，你不能那样做。

579
00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:01.640
Don't shake our baby.
别摇晃我们的宝宝。

580
00:24:01.820 --> 00:24:01.960
Yeah.
是啊。

581
00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:02.620
Okay.
好的。

582
00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:03.940
I've never heard that before.
我以前从没听说过这个。

583
00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:04.860
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

584
00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:05.440
Yeah.
是啊。

585
00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:06.400
I'm glad you said something.
很高兴你提到了。

586
00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:06.880
Me too.
我也是。

587
00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:10.080
I'm glad you said something.
很高兴你提到了。

588
00:24:12.180 --> 00:24:15.440
You guys, in our rewatch, I've shared this before.
各位，在我们的重温过程中，我之前分享过。

589
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:17.840
I absolutely love Ryan.
我绝对爱死瑞安了。

590
00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:20.860
I love the way BJ Novak plays the character of Ryan.
我喜欢BJ·诺瓦克饰演瑞安这个角色的方式。

591
00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:25.240
When I listened to that, his delivery is still so funny to me.
当我听到那段话时，他的演绎对我来说依然非常搞笑。

592
00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:26.740
We couldn't get through that scene.
我们当时根本无法顺利拍完那场戏。

593
00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:29.900
I mean, we busted up so many times.
我是说，我们笑场了太多次。

594
00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:35.800
I watched so many Pam versus Ryan clips last night.
昨晚我看了好多帕姆对战瑞安的片段。

595
00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:42.400
And I really would love so much to just make it an episode and bring BJ in here because it is so wonderful.
我真的非常希望能专门做一期节目，把BJ请过来，因为那实在太精彩了。

596
00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:44.700
That is the spinoff I want to watch.
那才是我想要看的衍生剧。

597
00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:48.160
BJ Novak is one of my most favorite people ever.
BJ·诺瓦克是我最喜欢的人之一。

598
00:24:48.160 --> 00:24:49.060
I would love that.
我太赞同了。

599
00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:54.460
And then there is Pam versus the entire Dunder Mifflin office.
然后还有帕姆对战整个邓德·米夫林办公室。

600
00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:56.720
I'm going to read this for you.
我要为你读一下这个。

601
00:24:57.040 --> 00:25:05.100
It's from the Niagara episode when Pam was pregnant and she asked everyone in the office if they could kind of tone it down on the smelly stuff.
这是出自《尼亚加拉大瀑布》那一集，当时帕姆怀孕了，她请求办公室里的每个人能不能稍微收敛一下那些有味道的东西。

602
00:25:05.300 --> 00:25:12.300
Like Phyllis with her perfume soaps and Meredith and her cigars and then Dwight's super smelly lunches.
比如菲利斯用的香皂，梅雷迪思抽的雪茄，还有德怀特那些味道特别冲的午餐。

603
00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:17.700
She's having really horrible morning sickness and she just said, can you guys just tone this down?
她当时孕吐非常严重，就说，你们能不能稍微克制一点？

604
00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:21.640
Well, no one wants to change their routines.
结果，没人愿意改变自己的习惯。

605
00:25:21.940 --> 00:25:26.940
So Pam has a talking head where she says, I don't think I'm asking for too much.
于是帕姆对着镜头说，我觉得我的要求并不过分。

606
00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:29.860
I guess it's just the end of courtesy in the workplace.
我想这大概就是职场礼仪的终结吧。

607
00:25:30.380 --> 00:25:32.440
And then it cuts to this scene.
然后镜头就切到了这一幕。

608
00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:35.140
Dwight is peeling a hard-boiled egg at his desk.
德怀特正坐在办公桌前剥一个水煮蛋。

609
00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:36.980
He sniffs it and takes a bite.
他闻了闻，然后咬了一口。

610
00:25:37.300 --> 00:25:41.720
Pam stares at him, picks up her trash can and pukes in it.
帕姆盯着他看，拿起垃圾桶就吐了进去。

611
00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:44.160
This causes a chain reaction.
这引发了一连串的连锁反应。

612
00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:51.140
Andy, Phyllis, Meredith, Aaron, Oscar, and Angela all proceed to throw up in various places in the office.
安迪、菲利斯、梅雷迪思、亚伦、奥斯卡和安吉拉全都开始在办公室的各个角落呕吐起来。

613
00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:53.740
Dwight stares, shocked at Pam.
德怀特震惊地盯着帕姆。

614
00:25:54.140 --> 00:25:57.660
Pam wipes her mouth with a satisfied look.
帕姆擦了擦嘴，露出了满意的神情。

615
00:25:57.900 --> 00:25:59.640
She took down the whole office.
她把整个办公室的人都给“干掉”了。

616
00:26:00.660 --> 00:26:02.040
That's some Pam sass.
这就是帕姆的傲娇时刻。

617
00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:06.520
And, you know, I'm really barely scratching the surface.
而且，你知道，我这还只是触及了皮毛而已。

618
00:26:06.720 --> 00:26:08.100
There's so much more Pam sass.
帕姆的傲娇时刻还有很多很多。

619
00:26:08.100 --> 00:26:10.940
But I want to end with one of my all-time favorites.
但我还是想以我个人最喜欢的一个片段来结尾。

620
00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:13.500
It is Pam versus Dwight.
那是帕姆对阵德怀特。

621
00:26:14.020 --> 00:26:16.000
It's one of the most stressful things you can do in life.
这是人生中最让人压力山大的事情之一。

622
00:26:16.160 --> 00:26:17.660
You'll probably just take it out on your kid.
你大概只会把气撒在孩子身上。

623
00:26:18.340 --> 00:26:19.420
Jim will turn to the drink.
吉姆会借酒消愁。

624
00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:21.260
The family will fall apart.
这个家庭会分崩离析。

625
00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:27.320
And 25 years from now, Cece will become world famous for stripping.
25年后，希希会因为跳脱衣舞而闻名世界。

626
00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:29.720
It's a sad story.
那是个悲伤的故事。

627
00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:31.680
I have another one.
我还有一个。

628
00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:32.720
We move.
我们搬家。

629
00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:34.300
The other tenants follow.
其他房客也跟着搬。

630
00:26:34.540 --> 00:26:38.440
The bank takes the building, takes your farm, takes your car, and beats the crap out of you.
银行收走大楼，收走你的农场，收走你的车，还要把你打个半死。

631
00:26:38.540 --> 00:26:39.560
Penniless, you die.
你身无分文，凄惨死去。

632
00:26:39.740 --> 00:26:43.640
And my daughter Cece dances on your grave, fully clothed.
然后我的女儿希希在你的坟头上跳舞，而且是穿着衣服跳的。

633
00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:46.400
That's such a good speech.
那段台词写得真好。

634
00:26:46.820 --> 00:26:47.740
That's so good.
太棒了。

635
00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:49.680
My God, our writers are so good.
天哪，我们的编剧真是太厉害了。

636
00:26:49.780 --> 00:26:50.880
That's such good writing.
那段剧本写得真好。

637
00:26:51.060 --> 00:26:51.720
Oh, my goodness.
噢，我的天哪。

638
00:26:52.120 --> 00:26:55.940
Well, that ends my Pam sass segment of All About Pam Beasley.
好了，关于“帕姆傲娇时刻”的专题就到此结束了。

639
00:26:55.940 --> 00:27:00.920
And now I want to move on to this fan question from Fanola Kay in the UK.
现在我想进入来自英国的粉丝Fanola Kay提出的问题。

640
00:27:01.340 --> 00:27:03.920
Which Pam moments are you proudest of?
你最引以为傲的帕姆时刻是哪些？

641
00:27:04.400 --> 00:27:11.480
Well, when I think about The Office, I mean, I'm just so proud of the whole show and everything.
嗯，想到《办公室》这部剧，我是说，我为整部剧以及其中的一切感到无比自豪。

642
00:27:11.660 --> 00:27:15.380
But there is one moment that I am most proud of.
但确实有一个时刻是我最引以为傲的。

643
00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:24.560
And it is the talking head at the end of the job when Jim peeks his head in and asks Pam out on a date.
那就是在《工作》那一集结尾的采访镜头，吉姆探进头来约帕姆出去约会的时候。

644
00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:26.480
Oh, and you tear up.
噢，你当时都热泪盈眶了。

645
00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:32.280
I think it's one of my finest acting moments of my whole career, frankly.
坦白说，我认为那是我整个职业生涯中最精彩的表演时刻之一。

646
00:27:32.620 --> 00:27:36.620
And I really credit Ken Kwapis for getting that performance out of me.
我真的要归功于肯·卡皮斯，是他激发出了我那样的表演。

647
00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:42.120
It was just, I mean, I don't even know how I did it.
当时的感觉就是，我是说，我甚至不知道自己是怎么做到的。

648
00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:49.540
And, you know, just as an audience, just someone watching it, because now I'm watching it just as a fan of the show.
而且，你知道，作为观众，作为一个观看者，因为我现在是以粉丝的身份在看这部剧。

649
00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:53.600
That moment is so pivotal and meaningful.
那一刻是如此关键且意义深远。

650
00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:56.860
And you did it perfect.
而且你演得太完美了。

651
00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:58.440
Like, perfect.
简直完美。

652
00:27:58.440 --> 00:28:00.200
It's so raw.
太真实了。

653
00:28:00.720 --> 00:28:09.600
And it really could only occur, like, if you gave me that scene in a movie and I had to just do that, I don't know if I could have done it.
而且这真的只有在那种情况下才可能发生，如果是在电影里给我这样一个场景让我去演，我不知道自己能不能演出来。

654
00:28:09.740 --> 00:28:17.760
But because I had the history of her story of years of playing this character, and I had that relationship with Ken Kwapis.
但因为我有多年扮演这个角色的背景故事，而且我和肯·夸皮斯（Ken Kwapis）之间也有那种关系。

655
00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:27.440
And so much of my reaction was from locking eyes with him and what he was giving me on the other side of the camera.
我的大部分反应都来自于和他对视，以及他在镜头另一端给我的反馈。

656
00:28:27.780 --> 00:28:28.180
Yeah.
没错。

657
00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:32.480
It was that look that, like, your dad gives you when he's proud of you.
那种眼神，就像你父亲为你感到骄傲时看你的眼神。

658
00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:33.560
Oh.
噢。

659
00:28:33.560 --> 00:28:35.520
And it just melted me.
那一刻我整个人都被融化了。

660
00:28:36.020 --> 00:28:40.200
So there were all of these circumstances that led to that moment happening.
所以是所有这些环境因素共同促成了那一刻的发生。

661
00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:42.800
And I love that we captured it.
我很高兴我们捕捉到了那一幕。

662
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.200
And I love that it was Ken in that moment with you.
我也很高兴那一刻陪在你身边的是肯。

663
00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:46.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

664
00:28:47.080 --> 00:28:51.380
Because he had been there since the very beginning.
因为他从一开始就在那里。

665
00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:52.000
Yes.
是的。

666
00:28:52.200 --> 00:28:53.200
That's so important.
这一点非常重要。

667
00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:57.340
He was as invested in my character story as I was.
他和我一样，对我的角色故事投入了同样多的心血。

668
00:28:57.500 --> 00:28:57.720
Yeah.
没错。

669
00:28:58.140 --> 00:28:58.360
Yeah.
是的。

670
00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:00.680
Oh, I love that moment, too.
噢，我也很喜欢那一幕。

671
00:29:00.680 --> 00:29:04.240
Well, lady, now it's my turn to do some sharing.
好了，女士，现在轮到我来分享一些东西了。

672
00:29:04.840 --> 00:29:09.940
Well, we've started this tradition of each sharing an area of interest about our character.
我们已经形成了一个传统，就是每个人都要分享一个关于自己角色的兴趣点。

673
00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:13.340
You know I love to title things, create structure.
你知道我喜欢给事物命名，建立结构。

674
00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:13.960
I know.
我知道。

675
00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:16.960
I love, like, our different ways of titling things.
我喜欢我们那种不同的命名方式。

676
00:29:17.100 --> 00:29:19.480
I'm like, Pam Sass, you're like area of intereSt.
我会说“帕姆的精髓”，而你会说“兴趣点”。

677
00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:19.920
Yes.
没错。

678
00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:29.020
Well, for my Pam Beasley area of interest, I really tried to think of things that I hadn't already shared on the podcaSt.
那么，关于我的帕姆·比斯利（Pam Beasley）兴趣点，我真的试着去想一些我还没在播客里分享过的事情。

679
00:29:29.020 --> 00:29:31.700
I mean, we've broken down all the episodes.
毕竟，我们已经拆解过所有的剧集了。

680
00:29:31.980 --> 00:29:32.160
Yeah.
没错。

681
00:29:32.360 --> 00:29:35.380
And I was really worried that I wouldn't have anything new to say.
我真的很担心自己没什么新鲜的东西可说了。

682
00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:37.960
Like that the first kiss was at the Dundies?
比如初吻是在邓迪奖（Dundies）颁奖礼上？

683
00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:40.000
Because I thought that was a pretty good one.
因为我觉得那已经算是一个很棒的点了。

684
00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:41.740
Why are you being so hard on yourself?
你为什么对自己要求这么严苛？

685
00:29:41.860 --> 00:29:42.240
Okay.
好吧。

686
00:29:42.540 --> 00:29:42.940
Okay.
好的。

687
00:29:43.600 --> 00:29:44.740
What else you got?
你还有什么别的吗？

688
00:29:45.160 --> 00:29:48.960
Well, I thought of two things that I could share about playing Pam Beasley.
嗯，我想到两件关于扮演帕姆·比斯利的事可以分享。

689
00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:52.260
Both of the things are actor prep that I did.
这两件事都是我做的演员准备工作。

690
00:29:52.260 --> 00:30:00.120
So the first thing is that when I'm prepping for a character, I sometimes go out in the world as that character.
第一件事是，当我在为角色做准备时，我有时会以角色的身份走进现实世界。

691
00:30:00.380 --> 00:30:06.460
Like I'll go grocery shopping or I'll do other tasks pretending to be in character.
比如我会去超市买东西，或者做些其他琐事，假装自己就是那个角色。

692
00:30:06.700 --> 00:30:07.800
Lady, you're so method.
女士，你太入戏了。

693
00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:10.920
What if your character was like a bank robber?
如果你的角色是个银行劫匪怎么办？

694
00:30:11.040 --> 00:30:13.280
You can't go out in the world as the bank robber.
你总不能以银行劫匪的身份走在街上吧。

695
00:30:13.380 --> 00:30:17.600
But you can because my character won't be robbing a bank the whole time.
但我可以，因为我的角色又不会一直都在抢银行。

696
00:30:17.800 --> 00:30:20.180
It'll just be a bank robber running errands.
那只会是一个去办杂事的银行劫匪。

697
00:30:20.280 --> 00:30:20.620
Yes.
没错。

698
00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:20.980
Okay.
好吧。

699
00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:21.600
Yes.
是的。

700
00:30:21.800 --> 00:30:26.780
So who am I when I go to the grocery store or how do I interact with the world?
那么，当我走进超市时，我是谁？或者说我是如何与这个世界互动的？

701
00:30:26.980 --> 00:30:29.340
So I went to the grocery store as Pam.
所以我当时以帕姆的身份去了杂货店。

702
00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:31.940
And I remember this very clearly.
我记得非常清楚。

703
00:30:32.540 --> 00:30:35.880
I was in line with my groceries and someone cut in front of me.
我正排队买东西，有人插到了我前面。

704
00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:37.820
How do you think Jenna feels about that?
你觉得珍娜对此会怎么想？

705
00:30:38.400 --> 00:30:41.840
Oh, Jenna would be like, excuse me, I'm standing here.
哦，珍娜会说，不好意思，我站在这儿呢。

706
00:30:41.960 --> 00:30:42.300
I would.
我会的。

707
00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:45.920
I would say, the end of the line is back there.
我会说，队尾在那边。

708
00:30:46.020 --> 00:30:46.460
Excuse me.
不好意思。

709
00:30:46.580 --> 00:30:46.680
Yeah.
没错。

710
00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:48.740
You'd be very fair, but you would let them know.
你会很讲道理，但你会让他们知道。

711
00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:49.160
Correct.
没错。

712
00:30:49.380 --> 00:30:49.580
Yes.
是的。

713
00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:52.760
Well, Pam doesn't say anything, apparently.
好吧，显然帕姆什么都没说。

714
00:30:53.060 --> 00:30:56.720
I was Pam and she just let this person cut in front of her.
我当时是帕姆，她就任由那个人插到了她前面。

715
00:30:56.940 --> 00:30:57.260
Right.
对。

716
00:30:57.620 --> 00:30:57.820
Yeah.
是啊。

717
00:30:58.080 --> 00:30:59.860
It was just an interesting thing.
这真是一件有趣的事。

718
00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:05.120
So it's like, how do you find out little details about how your character reacts and
所以就像是，你如何去挖掘关于你的角色在世界中如何反应和

719
00:31:05.120 --> 00:31:06.060
interacts in the world?
互动的细节呢？

720
00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:10.560
Which I thought was important because I knew that our show was going to have improvisation.
我觉得这很重要，因为我知道我们的剧会有即兴表演。

721
00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:16.600
And so I wanted to basically go out in the world and have people throw scenarios at me
所以我基本上想走到现实世界中，让人们给我出些状况，

722
00:31:16.600 --> 00:31:18.140
and see how Pam might react.
看看帕姆会如何反应。

723
00:31:18.340 --> 00:31:19.540
And it's just information.
这只是为了获取信息。

724
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:20.680
I just love this.
我太喜欢这个了。

725
00:31:20.800 --> 00:31:22.800
This is so thorough of you.
你考虑得真周全。

726
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:24.060
I love it.
我喜欢。

727
00:31:24.260 --> 00:31:30.440
I have to say one thing, one thing really quickly, which is one time I was standing in line for
我得说一件事，非常快地说一件事，就是有一次我排队看

728
00:31:30.440 --> 00:31:37.020
a movie and this lady cut in front of, like legit cut in front, so much so that the girl
电影，有个女士插到了我前面，真的是那种明目张胆地插队，以至于那个

729
00:31:37.020 --> 00:31:41.340
taking the tickets, like looked at me and then looked at her, like the line forms here,
检票的女孩看了看我，又看了看她，意思是队是从这儿排的，

730
00:31:41.580 --> 00:31:41.820
you know?
你知道吗？

731
00:31:41.940 --> 00:31:42.060
Yeah.
嗯。

732
00:31:42.060 --> 00:31:48.480
And she looked at me and the lady goes, I'm going to my movie.
她看着我，然后那个女士说，我要去看我的电影了。

733
00:31:48.640 --> 00:31:50.040
Like, what's the deal?
就像是，这算什么事儿？

734
00:31:50.680 --> 00:31:57.280
And I said to her, look, you cut in front of everyone, but clearly this is really important
我对她说，听着，你插到了所有人前面，但显然这对你来说真的很重要。

735
00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:57.920
to you.
就像是，你需要去看这场电影，而对我来说没那么重要。

736
00:31:58.240 --> 00:32:02.560
Like, you need to get to this movie and it's not important to me.
所以你为什么不去你的电影呢？

737
00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:04.120
So why don't you go to your movie?
她当时惊得目瞪口呆。

738
00:32:04.500 --> 00:32:06.500
She was like mouth agape.
是啊。

739
00:32:07.060 --> 00:32:07.180
Yeah.
那就是你处理这些事情的方式。

740
00:32:08.560 --> 00:32:10.000
That's how you handle those.
没错。

741
00:32:10.020 --> 00:32:10.200
Yeah.
插队的人。

742
00:32:10.580 --> 00:32:11.480
Line cutters.
我只是羞辱了他们。

743
00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:12.880
I just shamed them.
是的，没错。

744
00:32:13.120 --> 00:32:14.140
Yes, exactly.
我就像是，陈述事实，提供信息，队尾在那边。

745
00:32:16.060 --> 00:32:20.300
I'm like, matter of fact, information, the end of the line is back there.
很有礼貌，但是。

746
00:32:20.680 --> 00:32:21.740
Polite about it, but.
是啊。

747
00:32:22.260 --> 00:32:22.540
Yeah.
你知道的。

748
00:32:22.660 --> 00:32:22.860
You know.
嗯。

749
00:32:23.180 --> 00:32:23.400
Yeah.
是啊。

750
00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:23.920
Yeah.
没错。

751
00:32:24.100 --> 00:32:25.140
You're like, shame.
你就像是在说，真丢人。

752
00:32:26.740 --> 00:32:28.500
Clearly this is super important to you.
显然这对你来说非常重要。

753
00:32:28.600 --> 00:32:29.660
So why don't you have it?
那为什么你没有呢？

754
00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:30.800
We're going to let you have it.
我们打算让你拥有它。

755
00:32:31.040 --> 00:32:33.880
Well, interestingly enough, I also went to the movies as Pam.
嗯，有趣的是，我也曾以帕姆的身份去看过电影。

756
00:32:34.200 --> 00:32:34.600
You did?
你真的去过？

757
00:32:34.780 --> 00:32:35.300
Yes, I did.
是的，我去过。

758
00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:36.380
What did Pam go to see?
帕姆去看了什么电影？

759
00:32:36.580 --> 00:32:40.740
I don't remember what she went to see, but I have a very distinct memory that when she
我不记得她去看了什么，但我有段非常清晰的记忆，就是当她

